   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Small things that matter",
     "texto": [
      "Today we talk about jewellery, keepsakes and bathroom things.\n\n- **Jewellery:** a **joya** can be an **anillo** (on a finger), a **collar** (round the neck), a **pulsera** (on the wrist) or **pendientes** (on the ears). The material takes **de**: **de oro**, **de plata**.\n- **Llevar, ponerse, quitarse:** **llevar** is to have it on; **ponerse** is the action of putting it on; **quitarse** is the opposite.\n- **Keepsakes:** a **recuerdo** is both what you remember and the object you keep: «es un recuerdo de mi abuela».\n- **In the bathroom:** the **peine** and the **secador** are for your hair. The **perfume** and the **bolsa de aseo** travel with you.\n- **Make-up:** **pintarse** los labios. With body parts you use the article: **me pinto los labios**, not «mis labios».\n- **First aid:** a **tirita** is for a small cut."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "What it is made of and what you put on",
     "texto": [
      "Two things are worth knowing:\n\n- **The material** is said with **de**: un anillo **de oro**, un collar **de plata**, una puerta **de madera**.\n- **With the body and clothes** you use the article, not the possessive, when the verb is reflexive: **me pinto los labios**, **se pone el collar**, **nos lavamos las manos**.\n\nThree verbs help you talk about what you wear: **llevar** (to have it on), **ponerse** (to start wearing it) and **quitarse** (to stop wearing it)."
     ],
